    schema:description "About BJAK The original mission of BJAK is we believe people deserve smarter ways to plan, save and grow their money. This is the origin of our name. Started in 2019, we built the first mobile-first, insurance platform, enabling insurance to be accessible online by millions in the region. Today, its the leading insurance platform in Southeast Asia. Today, we are expanding ways to help people in the region — this includes spending, saving, investing, exchanging, travelling, and more. Our mission is help people get more from their money every day. We have teams working around the world, with over 20 nationalities from our offices and remotely, who truly enjoys their work. We are looking for the most talented and driven people we can find. We are looking for people who work for their passion, not counting hours. Who loves building great next-generation products, not status quo. Who cares about redefining how everyone around us can get the best financial applications, not for an exclusive few. If you're this person, we'd love to talk to you. About the Role The CEO - AI Investing will build and own an AI-native consumer investing business. The role will use AI to help users understand markets, make better investment decisions and manage their portfolios. What you will be doing Define the AI Investing proposition, product roadmap and business model. Build AI-native experiences across investment discovery, research, portfolio management and decision-making. Develop how AI should analyse information, surface opportunities and support users throughout the investment journey. Own P&L, assets, customers, engagement, revenue and unit economics. Work deeply with product, engineering and AI teams to build and improve the product. Build the core investing, product, technology and commercial teams. Expand into additional investment products and markets. What you will need Deep experience in investing, wealthtech, consumer fintech or investment products. Direct ownership of a meaningful investing product, business or P&L. Strong understanding of investment products, markets and consumer investing behaviour. Strong product judgement and understanding of how AI can improve investment research and decision-making. Experience building and scaling consumer technology products. Hands-on operating capability. Able to work directly through product, investment workflows, economics and customer behaviour. Location This is a hybrid role. You are expected to work from our local office at least 3 days per week, with the remaining days offering flexibility to work remotely. Candidates should be based in, or able to work from, the location where the role is advertised. Language English is our main working language across global teams. Strong English communication is required. Interview Process Our process is designed to move fast: 1. Online assessment or practical task 2. Role-specific interview 3. CEO / final round For strong candidates, we aim to complete the process and make an offer within 1 week from the start of the interview process. Candidates who complete assessments quickly will be prioritized. Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
