    schema:datePosted "2026-09-01"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Online marketplaces have never been this awesome. Join our team of passionate technology enthusiasts and e-commerce specialists in our state-of-the-art offices in Düsseldorf or Palma de Mallorca! We are currently seeking a highly skilled and experienced Data Analyst – Business Analyst with expertise in commercial side of the business to join our Business Intelligence & Data Analytics team. To ensure success as a Data Analyst - Business Analyst, you should possess passion for data, strong problem-solving and communication skills, and experience in a similar role. Join us to translate data and insights into actionable profit-enhancing strategies. Your Responsibilities Work closely with cross-functional teams (Commercial, Pricing, Tech&Product, Country Leads, Marketing etc.) to gather business requirements and translate them into BI solutions. Develop, own and further enhance reports, dashboards, and data visualizations to communicate key insights and performance metrics. Analyse large datasets to identify trends, patterns, and opportunities for optimization. Utilize statistical modelling methods to assess the potential impact of pricing strategies on profitability, marketing spent, replenishment or other commercial projects. Analyse data from diverse sources to gain insights into commercial strategies and market trends. Optimization and ongoing development of our BI landscape, systems and tools. Ensuring scalable data architecture, data integration and data processing. You've got Minimum of 4 years of hands-on experience in Business Analytics, Data Analytics, ideally in commercial strategies. Strong educational or practical background in Data Analytics, Data Science, Mathematics, Statistics, Finance, Economics, or a related field. Advanced level of proficiency in exploratory data analysis, and drive “so what” and business impact from data-driven insights Expert-level proficiency in Power BI, including DAX, data modeling, and creating interactive dashboards and reports. Strong knowledge of coding languages such as SQL, Python, or R, along with relevant frameworks. Good knowledge in common business intelligence software Experience working with structured and unstructured data, preferably on cloud-based data platforms. In-depth understanding of Pricing, Commercial, and E-commerce relevant KPIs and metrics, ideally within the e-commerce and retail/wholesale industry. Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy. Proactive, open-minded, and motivated mindset. Excellent communication skills with the ability to pitch ideas and effectively communicate insights to diverse audiences. We've got Over 70+ different nationalities and a diverse set of competencies A “greenfield” project – an agile environment with a start-up mentality, no bureaucracy, flat hierarchies and the courage to evaluate new approaches Strongly motivated, international and collaborative teams Hybrid working model within each team An international team in a modern offices in both Germany & Spain The opportunity for you to become part of a growing e-commerce company. Supportive and engaging people who are passionate about developing others and providing an environment to learn and grow Continuous development opportunities and exposure to a wide range of departments An international team of experts distributed all over Europe Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
