    schema:description "Position Jung von Matt HAMBURG is looking for a Senior Project Manager (m/f/d) – full-time what you bring You have many years of experience leading complex client relationships, ideally within client services, account management or project management in an agency environment. You are client-focused, identify opportunities and develop accounts strategically and commercially. You lead interdisciplinary teams with confidence, empathy and clarity. You are a strong senior advisor and a trusted sparring partner for C-level clients. You maintain oversight in complex situations, set priorities and make well-informed decisions. You combine strategic thinking with strong project management and execution skills. You work in a structured, proactive and responsible manner, even under pressure. You handle confidential information with the highest level of professionalism and discretion. You communicate confidently in both German and English, verbally and in writing. You thrive in dynamic agency environments and have a strong affinity for advertising, moving image and sports. Your responsibilities You take full responsibility for the strategic, operational and commercial leadership of key client accounts. You act as the primary point of contact for clients at senior management level. You develop integrated communication and brand solutions across all relevant advertising materials, with a focus on moving image. You lead teams, budgets, timelines and resources across all project phases. You identify opportunities within existing accounts and actively drive their development. You ensure the highest level of consulting, project and execution quality and long-term client satisfaction. You lead pitches, presentations and client decision-making processes. You continuously optimize processes, structures and workflows within your accounts and beyond. You act as a thought partner and contribute to the strategic, professional and cultural development of the agency. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
