    schema:datePosted "2026-09-02"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Position Jung von Matt NECKAR is looking for a Senior Social Media Manager (d/f/m). You know how to build brands and drive business on social? As a Senior Social Media Manager (d/f/m), you'll take strategic and commercial responsibility for complex social media accounts and campaigns. You develop innovative strategies, challenge briefs and guide projects from idea to execution. As a trusted sparring partner for clients and interdisciplinary teams, you set direction, drive quality and identify opportunities for innovation. That sounds like you? Read on. Your tasks: Taking strategic and commercial responsibility for complex social media accounts and campaigns Developing cross-platform and social-first strategies based on objectives, audiences and customer journeys Advising clients at eye level and presenting strategies and recommendations to senior stakeholders Leading campaigns, productions and workflows from concept to execution Managing budgets, KPIs and performance, including reporting and strategic recommendations Driving innovation through new platforms, technologies, trends and creative opportunities What we are looking for: Several years of experience in social media, ideally in an agency or creative environment Proven track record managing complex accounts with responsibility for performance, budgets and quality Excellent strategic, conceptual and analytical skills Strong understanding of social culture, platforms and creative possibilities Strong commercial awareness and confident budget management Excellent presentation, negotiation and client advisory skills, both in German and English What you can expect: Professional growth: Access extensive training opportunities, including language courses in German and English, along with a variety of internal programs for personal development Health and wellness: Receive a subsidized Wellpass membership and support for mental health through mindfulness sessions and coaching opportunities Family and lifestyle support: Utilize our Parents Program and bike leasing options Annual leave: Enjoy 30 days of vacation to recharge and maintain your creativity Exclusive discounts: Enjoy corporate benefits with employee discounts on various services and products Engaging events: Participate in unique activities like Cinema Tuesdays and our annual ski trip, the Brettertour Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
