    schema:description "Your mission The Applications team builds, maintains, and operates the solutions that collect high-quality sensor data from large freight and offshore vessels - data our customers rely on via SCADA, web, and other on-board applications. At the center of our work is the Software Engineering Center, our in-house backbone application used company-wide to design and configure software projects for vessels around the world. When something breaks, you're one of the people colleagues and customers turn to. You'll join a friendly, cross-functional team based near Hamburg, working in an agile, pragmatic way with short decision-making paths - and real ownership over what you build. What you'll do Own the development and ongoing evolution of the Software Engineering Center, from requirements through design, implementation, testing, and rollout Work directly with colleagues across departments to understand their needs and turn them into reliable features Troubleshoot operational issues and fix bugs - your code runs on systems used company-wide, so quality and reliability matter Be a go-to person for colleagues, service technicians when things go wrong Your profile Based in Hamburg, Germany, or currently residing elsewhere in Germany with willingness to relocate A relevant university degree in computer engineering or a related field, and/or solid professional experience 3–5 years building software with .NET (C#), with a track record of scalable, maintainable solutions Hands-on experience with CI/CD pipelines, Git/SVN, Bamboo/Jenkins, and Bitbucket A pragmatic, analytical mindset — you can take a messy technical problem and turn it into a clear plan Strong communication skills; you're comfortable explaining technical trade-offs to both engineers and nontechnical colleagues A customer-first, quality-driven approach to your work Fluent German (C1); good working English Why us? Be part of an exciting and pioneering maritime domain that's shaping the future of smart shipping and marine technology Embrace our \"You build it, you run it\" philosophy - take full ownership of your work and see your ideas come to life Benefit from an unlimited contract and a modern, inspiring workplace equipped with everything you need to thrive. Enjoy flexible working hours and the possibility of working remotely at least 2 days a week. Receive a comprehensive onboarding program and tailored training opportunities to support your professional development. Take advantage of a wide range of employee perks, including regular team events, a monthly Urban Sports Club membership allowance, German language course, company bike leasing, subsidized public transport tickets, mindfulness and meditation programs, and so much more! Contact Hoppe Marine GmbH Anne Wiedenhoff Kieler Straße 318 22525 Hamburg +49 (0)40 561 949 – ----- Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
