    schema:description "This position is based in Barcelona, Spain. The Tax Engine team is hiring a Sr. Indirect Tax expert with deep Europe, North America or Brazil expertise to join our Global Tax Calculation Services team based in Barcelona. The Global Tax Calculation Services Program is comprised of tax professionals and software engineers that are responsible for providing end-to-end global transaction tax calculation solutions (sales and use taxes, value-added taxes, good and services taxes, and other consumption taxes). The individual in this role will contribute with critical tax research and classification work for complex Indirect Tax landscape and for Europe VAT product and services taxability research, taking ownership on end-to-end cross-functional tax-related projects and process improvements. This position will work closely with local business partners and rest of members of the tax department providing guidance and support to Global Product Classification. The role also requires fluent communication with Product Classification Specialists to provide support on their specific needs to be incorporated into the technical solutions. This position is office-based. Amazon encourages open communication about unique needs for flexible arrangements Key job responsibilities * Supporting and maintaining critical Tax Indirect Tax content across Europe, North America and Brazil. * Supporting dual tax regime operations during the 2026-2032 transition period in Brazil * Supporting and providing ongoing maintenance and enhancements to tax calculation software; * Providing support to the end-to-end Global transaction tax calculation solutions for a broad array of products and services * Supporting internal and external Audits * Providing technical advice on indirect tax rates applicable to Amazon’s catalogue based on the research of tax laws, regulations and jurisdiction changes * Supporting local business partners and tax department members with decisions on product taxability matters * Leverage ontology modeling skills (OWL – Web Ontology Language) to support the engineering team in structuring and formalizing tax classification knowledge, enabling more accurate and scalable taxonomy representations within our technical systems * Participating in team operational excellence programs and process improvements * Actively participate in selected projects throughout their life-cycle - 5+ years of Brazilian Indirect Tax experience or EU VAT esperience working in Big 4 advisory firm, law firm, or multi-national tax department - Bachelor's degree in Tax, Accounting, Law, Economics, Business Administration or related field - Strong written and verbal communication skills in English; additional languages is a plus - Indirect Tax knowledge (ICMS, IPI, PIS and COFINS); - Experience with Brazilian Tax Reform (Complementary Law 214/2025) - CBS, IBS, IS implementation - Experience maintaining and operating transaction tax calculation software (e.g. Vertex) - Experience in tax content development, rule creation, or tax research management for technology platforms - Fluency in Portuguese - Proficiency in other languages would be an advantage Amazon is an equal opportunities employer. We believe passionately that employing a diverse workforce is central to our success. We make recruiting decisions based on your experience and skills. We value your passion to discover, invent, simplify and build. Protecting your privacy and the security of your data is a longstanding top priority for Amazon. Please consult our Privacy Notice ( https://www.amazon.jobs/en/privacy_page ) to know more about how we collect, use and transfer the personal data of our candidates. Our inclusive culture empowers Amazonians to deliver the best results for our customers. If you have a disability and need a workplace accommodation or adjustment during the application and hiring process, including support for the interview or onboarding process, please visit https://amazon.jobs/content/en/how-we-hire/accommodations for more information. If the country/region you’re applying in isn’t listed, please contact your Recruiting Partner." ;
